<p>Because Seguin is in Guadalupe County, the Hays County figures elsewhere on this site do not describe it directly. National Weather Service event summaries do document several significant events in and around Seguin:</p>
<h3>October 30, 2015: the Geronimo tornado</h3>
<p>On the morning of October 30, 2015, an <a href="https://www.weather.gov/media/ewx/wxevents/ewx-20151031.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">EF-2 tornado with estimated peak winds of 111–120 mph</a> developed southwest of Geronimo, north of Seguin, and tracked about 8.25 miles toward the New Braunfels airport. The NWS survey found about 20 homes damaged and about 5 destroyed, with damage ranging from lost roofing material to complete removal of roof structures, plus damaged garages, barns, trailers, and farm equipment. The same morning, a separate EF-1 tornado began in Guadalupe County near Centerpoint Road and Old Zorn Road and moved into Hays County.</p>
<h3>October 1998: Guadalupe River flooding</h3>
<p>During the October 17–18, 1998 floods, the NWS reports that <a href="https://www.weather.gov/ewx/wxevent-1998flood" target="_blank" rel="noopener">homes were washed off their foundations along the Guadalupe River from Canyon Lake to Seguin</a>. River flooding is generally excluded from homeowners policies, which is why flood insurance matters for river-area properties.</p>
<h3>February 2021: Winter Storm Uri</h3>
<p>NWS spotters reported <a href="https://www.weather.gov/media/ewx/wxevents/ewx-20210218.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3.0 inches of snow just south-southwest of Seguin on February 15</a> and another inch on February 18, during more than a week of freezing weather that led to burst pipes across the region.</p>
